  "thag16.6:7.4": "",
  "thag16.6:7.5": "This is of course a reference to the first sermon (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/sn56.11/en/sujato'>SN 56.11</a>). ",
  "thag16.6:8.1": "",
  "thag16.6:8.2": "",
  "thag16.6:8.3": "",
  "thag16.6:8.4": "",
  "thag16.6:8.5": "",
  "thag16.6:9.1": "The title “General of the Dhamma” belongs to Sāriputta (<a href='https://suttacentral.net/ud2.8/en/sujato#16.2'>Ud 2.8:16.2</a>, <a href='https://suttacentral.net/thag18.1/en/sujato#33.1'>Thag 18.1:33.1</a>). ",
  "thag16.6:9.2": "",
  "thag16.6:9.3": "",
  "thag16.6:9.4": "",
  "thag16.6:10.1": "",
  "thag16.6:10.2": "",
  "thag16.6:10.3": "",
  "thag16.6:10.4": "",
  "thag16.6:10.5": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Anujāta</i> is said at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/iti74/en/sujato#4.1'>Iti 74:4.1</a> to be a child who “takes after” the good qualities of their parents. ",
  "thag16.6:11.1": "As at <a href='https://suttacentral.net/mn91/en/sujato#31.5'>MN 91:31.5</a>. ",
  "thag16.6:11.2": "",
  "thag16.6:11.3": "",
  "thag16.6:11.4": "",
  "thag16.6:12.1": "",
  "thag16.6:12.2": "",
  "thag16.6:12.3": "",
  "thag16.6:12.4": "<i lang='pi' translate='no'>Abhiṇhaso</i> means “repeatedly”. Here the force of the saying is, I think, “It is hard enough to encounter a Buddha even once, let alone repeatedly.” ",
